            <ArticleTitle>Aneurysm of the left main coronary artery without obstructive disease: report of a case presenting with severe unstable angina and treated with systemic thrombolysis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>306-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A fusiform aneurysm of the left main coronary artery without associated obstructive disease was detected in a 77-year-old patient with severe unstable angina treated with systemic thrombolysis. The authors emphasize the following features: (1) unusual location of the aneurysm, (2) absence of concomitant obstruction in this age group, and (3) clinical efficacy of thrombolysis and subsequent long-term oral anticoagulation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
